<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murong Chong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 386</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-xianbei">Murong</a> Chong was a prince of the deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/former-yan">Former Yan</a> house who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> rising against Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-river">Battle of Fei River</a>. Taking over from his brother Murong Hong in 384, he captured and plundered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> in 385 and proclaimed himself emperor of the state later called Western Yan. His followers, eager to return east, killed him in 386.</p></div>
